Ignoring the tools you have to pay for, some of the common
tools are:

*stat; iostat, vmstat, netstat, etc.  These are included
in the base system.  They just display text data, but
suitable filtering software could probably generate
graphs.

Monitor - This collects data in a documented format, which
can be processed as you see fit.  The data files can also
be replayed using the same interface (Curses based) that
it uses to display live data.

Collect - I think it has some of its own graph generation
capabilities.  Whether it is suitable for direct inclusion
into a web page is something I can't comment on.

