To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Recent Spam Warnings
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653755322484

Hi Tru64 admins!

(Yes, I know this list is not for discussions - 
I hope such a situation will not arise again.)

Jim Fitzmaurice wrote:
> [...] and others that I'm afraid to look at because the new virus 
> exploits a MIME hole. You don't have to open the message, 
> just highlight it in outlook and the preview feature does the rest, [...]

1) In my company, we officially got the hint to _disable_ 
   Outlook's "preview" feature for this very reason 
   (In the German version, click the third pull-down menu "Ansicht" 
   and remove the tick at "Vorschaufenster" - for other languages, 
   please find your corresponding place).

2) Jim (as well as several others, day by day) posted in HTML, 
   which (IMHO: unluckily) is displayed by (most or all) readers. 
   I would like to see all mail (at least on this list) to use plain 
   text only, for security reasons like these. 
   (And I would like to configure my Netscape not to show HTML, 
   if I only found a way to do so.)

I wish you all not to incur any damage from the current virus wave 
(and to enjoy your weekend),

Joerg Bruehe

-- 
Joerg Bruehe, SQL Datenbanksysteme GmbH, Berlin, Germany
     (speaking only for himself)
mailto: joerg@sql.de

