Managers,

Yesterday I got called into fix a dead 2100.

DU4.0B
Oracle 7.3
2GB system disk
Raid 5 SWXCR data disk

No administrator for the system in the last 2 years. =20

No /,/usr,/var backup (or they don't know where it is). =20

No one knows what format the oracle backups were made in, or how complete they =
are, but they do make one every day.

No DU4.0B CDs (I have DU4.0D, so I'm going to try to upgrade to it.)

No Oracle CDs, no Oracle docs.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Anyway, the main disk died a partial death.  fsck moved a couple hundred files =
into lost+found and deleted a lot more. =20

The /etc directory was cleared by fsck, so what is left is in lost+found.

The fstab file is gone.  (I did recover the license database!!!)

I moved the old bootdisk and put in a new disk at dka0.  I have installed =
DU4.0D on it.  I only have the minimum set of software and kernel sets =
installed.

It seems to be fine and I can mount the old bootdisk, but I can't see the SWXCR =
disk yet. =20

(I have never worked with SWXCR, so it is likely something I am doing wrong.)

I can do a dd if=3D/dev/re0c of=3D/dev/null and the raid 5 set seems to work, =
but if I try 'disklabel -r re0', I get an error message about there not being a =
disklabel.

I did install a SWXCR kit that allowed me to do a parity check and the it shows =
the raid set has no parity errors, so I assume that it still has data on it.

The SWXCR kit came from the DU40.B install, so I hope it doesn't hurt anything.

I also tried to install the SWXCR mgt gui kit, but it complains that it needs =
the c++ shared libraries installed first.  I don't think DU4.0D has a kit like =
that.  I did install a c++ class shared library kit, but it did not help.

What do I do next???

Do I need to somehow tell the OS how the SWXCR disks are configured??

Are there some SWXCR related config files I could try to recover from the old =
disk??


