Every once in a while, I have a situation with our print queues on our ES40 
Tru64 4.0F machine.  When a printer requires some attention (i.e. paper 
jam), the print queue needs to be restarted before the jobs will start 
printing.  This does not happened all of the time and is difficult to 
reproduce.  This particular printer is a HP LaserJet 8100 with a JetDirect 
card (Firmware Rev. G.08.04).  This is not the only printer that has had 
this issue, but this is one that I caught the following in the debug log 
file.  Also, I included the printcap entry.

Apr  2 09:11:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: DEBUG -- openpr: entered openpr(), printer 
la_pick1
Apr  2 09:11:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: DEBUG -- openpr: LP is null in 
/etc/printcap, RM is lj8000c, printer la_pick1
Apr  2 09:11:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: DEBUG -- getport: entered getport(), rhost 
lj8000c
Apr  2 09:24:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: INFO -- abort_signal: received signal 15, 
aborting current job
Apr  2 09:24:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: DEBUG -- writeStatus: status file update, 
printer la_pick1: Tue
Apr  2 09:24:40 2002: Apr  2 09:24:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: INFO -- 
abort_signal: exiting...
Apr  2 09:24:40 mega1 lpd[8709]: INFO -- printjob_exit: breaking promise to 
process all queued print jobs since this daemon

lp3|lj8000c|la_pick1:\
         :lf=/usr/adm/lp3err:\
         :lp=:\
         :rm=lj8000c:\
         :rp=text:\
         :sh:\
         :mx#0:\
         :sd=/usr/spool/lpd3:

Thank you,

