servers between two NIC cards.&nbsp;&nbsp;What we want is to add a third =
card to=20
the systems...can this be added to the existing NetRAIN set?&nbsp; And =
if so,=20
would it be as simple as:</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;=20
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; /sbin/ifconfig =
nr0=20
10.0.202.37&nbsp; netmask 255.255.255.0 add ee0,ee1,ee2</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2></FONT>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2>The other question is about NetRAIN=20
functionality.&nbsp; I remember a while ago a Compaq support guy said =
that=20
NetRAIN would be able to do load sharing at some point in the =
future.&nbsp; Has=20
this been implemented yet?&nbsp; Could we run load sharing on the three=20
cards?&nbsp; Or two cards?&nbsp; Or is it still just a simple failover=20
mechanism?&nbsp; It just seems silly to have three cards in the system, =
and=20
having two of them idle all the time.&nbsp; Anyway, thanks in advance.=20
</FONT></DIV>
<DIV><FONT face=3DArial size=3D2><BR>Jonathan Williams<BR>Unix Systems=20
Administrator<BR>The Shubert Organization, =
Inc.</FONT></DIV></BODY></HTML>

