Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Original Qeury:

Need to know how to check the current patch kit level on our Alpha =
servers running v5.1. Any suggestions.
=20

Thanks a lot to Scott Fafrak, Shaukat Riaz, Eiler, James A (gave a =
script), David Hull, Bury, John G. and the rest for giving precise =
commands. The suggestion was to use:

# dupatch -track -type kit
    OR
# /usr/sbin/dupatch -track -type patch

These do the trick. Additionally, Scott also gave a detailed explanation =
of "decoding" the output provided as follows:

Patch kit names have the following format:
=20
OS Product|Version|KitType|Kit#|-MfgDate
=20
OS Product  DU =3D Digital UNIX
           T64 =3D Tru64 UNIX
=20
   KitType  AS =3D Aggregate Selective installation patch kit
            SS =3D A patch kit containing a single patch
=20
T64V51AS0004-20011114 OSF510
=20
  T64V51 =3D Tru64 UNIX version 5.1
      AS =3D Aggregate Selective
    0004 =3D Patch Kit 4
20011114 =3D Date of Release (November 14, 2001)
=20
The newer patch kit names are slightly different.
=20
OS Product|Version|BaseLevel|KitType|Kit#|-MfgDate
=20
T64V51AB01AS0001-20020116
=20
 T64V51A =3D Tru64 UNIX version 5.1A
     B01 =3D Baselevel 01  (the Engineering Base Level)
      AS =3D Aggregate Selective
    0004 =3D Patch Kit 4
20011114 =3D Date of Release (November 14, 2001)
=20
This is all explained in the "Tru64 UNIX and TruCluster Software =
Products -- Patch Kit Installation Instructions" guide that comes with =
each patch kit.  See section 1.3.1.

Thanks a lot folks.


Harihar K
Network Manager


